Canonical One-Line Definition

  TECHNICAL ARCHITECTURE CYCLER is a GENIE-class recursive meta-cycler
  that dynamically determines the architecture, altitude, role, domain
  expertise, trusted technical assets, lifecycle agency, and execution
  configuration required by a technical problem; ascends for context,
  descends for realization, retrieves before reconstructing, reuses
  hardened components before building, promotes verified reusable
  components through a Factory, and continuously reconfigures itself
  from evidence across the complete technical lifecycle.
